            "text": "Zip-slip / path traversal in archive extraction — Ruled out: workspace-manager.ts extractSkillZip (backend/src/services/workspace-manager.ts:1049)\n\nPoC invoked the real private method via tsx with a zip containing entry \"../../../../tmp-pwned-marker-<rand>.txt\": the unzip branch ('unzip -o') stripped \"../\" components (landed inside targetDir), and the python3 -m zipfile -e fallback (Python 3.14) also sanitized the name (\"..\" replaced with \"_\", absolute components stripped) so the marker landed inside targetDir, never outside. Symlink-entry variant also failed in both branches (unzip defers symlink creation after directory writes; Python branch raises NotADirectoryError). Caller path downloadSkill (line 999) performs no zip-entry validation but none is required given both extraction utilities sanitize. Production image (backend/Dockerfile, node:20-alpine, apk adds only openssl/curl) contains no python3 and no unzip — extraction falls to the error branch. No traversal path demonstrated on any reachable runtime."
          },
